    "b-50-interaction-model-cross-surface-standard-2": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-cross-surface-standard-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The editor uses consistent gestures for selection, dragging, and annotations. The cross-surface convention is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Core Annotate-Agent UX",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "../docs/annotate-agent-ux.md"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; this page defines its Prompt Kit behavior."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-the-surface-renders-a-st-3": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-the-surface-renders-a-st-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The surface renders a structured document, and every pointer gesture acts on\nstructure. The address system is node ids, rings, and runs, not lines or\ncharacters, and ONE BOUNDARY splits the vocabulary, Notion-style, with no\nmodifier: plain gestures within a unit edit text, and the same gestures\ncrossing unit boundaries act on structure. Command is annotate mode's modifier\nonly, in edit mode Cmd+click is a plain click."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-divider-4": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-divider-4",
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {},
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-gesture-language-5": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-gesture-language-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Gesture Language"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-gesture-result-6": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-gesture-result-6",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Gesture",
          "Result"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Hover",
            "The one drag handle appears at the unit under the pointer"
          ],
          [
            "Click",
            "Caret / inline edit ONLY, never a block selection (caret-first)"
          ],
          [
            "Shift+click on a bullet",
            "Extend a contiguous item-range selection"
          ],
          [
            "Plain drag WITHIN one unit's text",
            "NATIVE browser text selection; a release confined to one editable row opens the inline editor with the dragged range pre-selected (type to replace)"
          ],
          [
            "Plain drag CROSSING unit boundaries",
            "OBJECT selection: the anchor-to-pointer row band live-resolves to a structural run (ring) on every move, kept on release"
          ],
          [
            "Plain drag inside the selection ring",
            "Move the selected run"
          ],
          [
            "Backspace / Delete (selection active, no editor open)",
            "Remove the run as one transaction"
          ],
          [
            "Escape / plain click elsewhere",
            "Clear the selection (Escape mid-drag abandons the band)"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-a-unit-is-the-list-item-7": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-a-unit-is-the-list-item-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A unit is the list item under the pointer or, failing that, the owning block\nnode. The drag stays completely inert, native selection and click-to-edit\nuntouched, until the pointer leaves the pressed unit; only then does the\nsurface clear the native selection and suppress text selection, and only for\nthe remainder of that gesture. A drag that crosses out and ends back on its\nanchor unit rings just the anchor unit (the drag route to a single-block\nselection; the grip remains the explicit single-block handle)."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-caret-first-clicks-8": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-caret-first-clicks-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Caret-First Clicks"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-clicking-or-typing-in-te-9": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-clicking-or-typing-in-te-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Clicking or typing in text is a CARET gesture, Notion-style: the caret plus\nthe unit-scoped edit wash (hover strength) is the entire treatment, no\nselection fill, no accent rail, no gutter tint. Placing the caret never\nselects the block it lands in; if a block selection exists when the caret\nlands (click, arrow-key caret hop, typing on a selected block), the selection\nis CLEARED, not retargeted. Commits made while an edit session is live also\nsuppress the change callback's selection echo, so hosts cannot re-select the\nedited block on a keystroke."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-explicit-selection-keeps-10": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-explicit-selection-keeps-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Explicit selection keeps its reach: non-editable rows (close tags, attributed\nopen tags, code fences), the block grip, outline clicks, and queue focus rows\nstill select through the host's selection callback. Selection paint follows\n\"flood never, rail for extent\" with one container rule, CONTAINERS NEVER\nSTRIPE: a selected section fills exactly its own open/close tag rows; a\nselected LIST paints no per-row fill at all (its rendered rows are its\nitems'), keeping only the full-extent rail."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-quiet-panels-follow-the-11": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-quiet-panels-follow-the-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Quiet panels follow the caret by DERIVATION: the surface reports the edit\nsession's enclosing node, and the shell's details zone shows the explicit\nselection if one exists, else that entry, without writing selection state or\npainting selection chrome."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
