      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-at-most-one-drag-handle-15": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-at-most-one-drag-handle-15",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "At most ONE drag handle exists at any moment: the handle of the deepest"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-draggable-unit-under-the-16": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-draggable-unit-under-the-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  draggable unit under the pointer, floating at that unit's left content\n  edge, the indentation margin for a nested bullet, the gutter for a\n  top-level block."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-item-rows-resolve-to-the-17": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-item-rows-resolve-to-the-17",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Item rows resolve to the ITEM (bullets are draggable units in their own"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-right-every-other-row-18": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-right-every-other-row-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  right); every other row resolves to its owning block. A list never owns a\n  hover handle, because all of its rendered rows are its items'."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-dragging-a-unit-carries-19": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-dragging-a-unit-carries-19",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Dragging a unit carries its children, so multi-line items move whole."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-the-block-handle-doubles-20": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-the-block-handle-doubles-20",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The block handle doubles as the block-menu trigger; item handles are"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-drag-only-glyph-sizes-e-21": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-drag-only-glyph-sizes-e-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  drag-only. Glyph sizes encode the hierarchy (block larger, item smaller)."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-the-ghost-is-a-compact-t-22": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-the-ghost-is-a-compact-t-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The ghost is a compact token, not a copy of the block: the unit's first\nrendered line, DOM-faithful (entities decoded exactly as displayed), plus a\nmuted \"+N more\" for multi-line drags. The thin drop indicator and the dimmed\nsource rows are the placement feedback."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-item-reorders-and-block-23": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-item-reorders-and-block-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Item reorders and block-run moves each commit as one undoable transaction."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-structural-selection-24": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-structural-selection-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structural Selection"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-a-covered-row-band-a-pl-25": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-a-covered-row-band-a-pl-25",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A covered row band (a plain drag's anchor-to-pointer rows, a shift-click"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-range-s-extent-resolves-26": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-range-s-extent-resolves-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  range's extent) resolves to the SHALLOWEST contiguous sibling run that\n  exactly covers the rows: bullets within one list select an item run;\n  crossing a list boundary promotes to the block run at the common parent (a\n  partial list promotes to the whole list); a band across sections selects\n  the top-level run. The result is one object in the AST."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-the-selection-paints-as-27": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-the-selection-paints-as-27",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The selection paints as ONE ring overlay, not per-row washes; hover washes,"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-accent-bars-and-gutter-28": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-accent-bars-and-gutter-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  accent bars, and gutter tints are suppressed inside it. One ring = one\n  object."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-the-run-moves-by-draggin-29": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-the-run-moves-by-draggin-29",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run moves by dragging its body (plain drag anywhere inside the ring) or"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-by-grabbing-any-handle-i-30": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-by-grabbing-any-handle-i-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  by grabbing any handle inside it, both are the same group drag. Backspace\n  or Delete removes it. Both are single transactions; one undo restores."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-selection-state-survives-31": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-selection-state-survives-31",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Selection state survives host re-renders by VALIDATION, not identity: hosts"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-rebuild-the-prompt-objec-32": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-rebuild-the-prompt-objec-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  rebuild the prompt object every render, so the state is kept while the\n  document still materializes the run and retired only when it genuinely\n  cannot."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-interaction-model-no-drag-draws-a-selectio-33": {
      "id": "b-50-interaction-model-no-drag-draws-a-selectio-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "No drag draws a selection rectangle, and there is no modifier-click unit\nselection: the selection gesture is the modifier-free plain drag across unit\nboundaries, live-resolved through the row-band rule on every pointer move."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
